{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/326060-advice-sought-for-new-campaign","id":326060,"title":"Advice sought for new campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-30T08:53:02-08:00","id":326060,"title":"Advice sought for new campaign","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hi</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">starting a CtL campaign in the new year,I have run a fair amount of old WOD and played a lot of nWOD, but I have not run CtL before and would appreciate suggestions and thoughts from more experienced players and GMs. It's replacing a campaign that is coming to a climax after 5 years, I am hoping this one will have similar longevity so advice for the 'long game' is especially welcome.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the start</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the majority of players won't know itsCtL; when they create their characters, I have told them we are playing mortals nwod game, for that matter I shall </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>run it </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">as a mortal NWOD game, with their the inquisitive parasychologists, psychics and nervous student interns getting peek behind the curtain of the WOD for three or four stories, letting them build up and get to know their characters, forge some mundane connection, learn the fundamental game mechanics etc, then swoosh; a 'haunted' house story that leads straight to Durance. I have a 'ringer' set up, a player who knows the general thrust of the campaign opening, who's ready to have their character replaced by a fetch earlier in the plot and work IC to lead the pcs to their doom when required.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would appreciate some thoughts on running durance and escape, do I go for straight narrative, vignettes, a mixture? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 of my 5 players don't know CtL at all , all their going to know what I show and tell them and they figure out experimentaly. The other two know it in passing but not deta</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hi</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">starting a CtL campaign in the new year,I have run a fair amount of old WOD and played a lot of nWOD, but I have not run CtL before and would appreciate suggestions and thoughts from more experienced players and GMs. It's replacing a campaign that is coming to a climax after 5 years, I am hoping this one will have similar longevity so advice for the 'long game' is especially welcome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the start</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the majority of players won't know its going to be CtL when they create their characters, I have told them we are playing mortals nwod game, for that matter I shall </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>run it </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">as a mortal NWOD game, with their the inquisitive parasychologists, psychics and nervous student interns getting peek behind the curtain of the WOD for three or four stories, letting them build up and get to know their characters, forge some mundane connection, learn the fundamental game mechanics etc, then, swoosh, a 'haunted' house story that leads straight to Durance. I have a 'ringer' set up, a player who knows the general thrust of the campaign, who's ready to have their character replaced by a fetch earlier in the plot and work IC to lead the pcs to their doom when required.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would appreciate some thoughts on running durance and escape, do I go for straight narrative, vignettes, a mixture? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 of my 5 players don't know CtL at all , all their going to know what I show and tell them. The other two know it in passing but not detail so I would also appreciate any thoughts on ways to demonstrate in IC key concepts of the game for a bunch of 'Fresh' changelings and their players.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2567-joedylan","user":"Joedylan","date":". 11-30-2014, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2567-joedylan","name":"Joedylan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:17:03-08:00","id":326086,"title":"","content":"Holy crap dude, go in and kill your size. I feel like I'm being buried by dalmatians left in a Stranger's library too long.<br /> <br /> Let me see what I can say once I recover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:31:13-08:00","id":326095,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> <br /> It's <i>hard</i> to run a durance for players. Namely because the time is more or less marked by stripping agency from them and imposing characteristics on them. It's even harder to do when you're trying to hide the buy-in a little bit, as players who know that the Keeper is supposed to touch them there or that fire coming out of their mouth is 'okay' narratively tend to play along better.<br /> <br /> What you want to do is play a mix of vignettes that allow consequences to just brew and settle, and play this like you would a group of people who may not realize they're working for a shady bunch. The Keeper gives them food, saying it'll let them breathe water for the upcoming mission, and as time goes on, they realize they permanently have gills. The Keeper tells them they're valuable commodities to his work, but as they play they realize they're filling menial labor. Stuff like that.The key thing is &quot;Keep up player agency&quot;. The player should always have a choice, even if the hidden reality is that their choices will always betray them at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-30-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:31:32-08:00","id":326096,"title":"","content":"Whoops, thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2567-joedylan","name":"Joedylan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T13:11:27-08:00","id":326225,"title":"","content":"Honest Opinion:<br /> <br /> Your intro can work well. Given the nature of Changeling, the &quot;start as mortals&quot; thing works a lot less well than, say, Vampire, Geist or even Werewolf or Mage. This introduction could work well, depending...you know your group.<br /> <br /> A major creative thing for players has often been designing the sort of Faerie they want, and the sort of Durance they want, or at least, the sort of Durance they are comfortable with, as players. One of the very best things about Changeling is mixing and matching Seemings and Kiths and Courts to make exactly the sort of Faerie you want to play. What I strongly recommend is run your intro, but then let players consider their own Durance and Keeper and &quot;build&quot; their own Faerie. It runs the risk that they will make a character and then wish they made a different sort because they fall in love with, say, Darklings, but if the mystery aspect is important to you at the beginning, you may well feel that risk is worth it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T15:31:40-08:00","id":326326,"title":"","content":"Or you can just run with your intro, show them they got to the Faerie and the said to players - &quot;here, look on those Seeming and Kiths and choose what would you like to make your PC in to&quot;. Then move action just <b>after</b> they left the Keeper and retrospectively in the chronicle make scenes about how exactly Durance fall on PCs. If in now, on Earth, they are hunting for Hedge beast, make the scene about their hunting made in their Durance. Or any other that could nicely add up with presently plot. Think of it as <a href=\"http://youtu.be/KTu8iDynwNc\" target=\"_blank\">LOST</a> with Lost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I plan to run this in mine coming game also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}